  "details": "December 13th update brought an unneeded change to the compatibility of devices, specifically how the game treats unsupported (ones with less than 6GB) devices.\n\nBefore, you could still play worlds on unsupported devices. You were given a warning about a device being unsupported. Your unsupported device could crash at some point, but you were warned that that would happen.\n\nNow, you are completely unable to play worlds on those unsupported devices. Whenever you click on a world or the Play! button, you only get a message that the device is unsupported and that one should get VRChat on other platforms.\n\nI can't state how limiting unsupported devices breaks stuff what I do personally. I tested worlds and avatars immediately after uploading to unity without booting up vrchat on a different device. When I translated a language string I could go in game where ever I am and look at the string to know if it's correct or not. The fact that it doesn't work in a single update is annoying and should be reverted to how it has been before.\n\nThis is somewhat anti consumer in my opinion. I do not want to be forced to buy a better device or use a different device because developers decided so. I know the limitations of my device, respected the warning and never complained when it crashed (which was a rarity). I understand that people kept sending crash reports from unsupported devices, but they were absolutely warned.\n\nPlease revert it to how it was before.",
